there's no reason to believe that attack skill advances were intended any 
differently. Ordinarily, the change from ray to targetted effects is 
positive: you can usually see your opponent, which doesn't have to be in a 
straight line from you for you to hit it. However, when you can't see your 
opponent, the spell becomes worthless, which it wasn't as a ray spell. This 
I consider to be an obvious bug.

